From: zibao <zibao@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: core: ignore user keepalives while suspended

The core PM notifier pings the watchdog for the last time on
PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and then cancels the keepalive hrtimer and worker.  A
userspace keepalive (WDIOC_KEEPALIVE) that reaches the driver just after
that cancellation re-arms the pretimeout hrtimer: the hrtimer then fires
in the middle of s2idle and panics the kernel.

Measured on a H96 Max H618 (sunxi-wdt, s2idle, systemd RuntimeWatchdogSec
15 s): a 60 s sleep armed with rtcwake panics with "watchdog pretimeout
event" even though the driver stopped the counter before the dpm phase.
With the userspace watchdog closed (no keepalives), the same sleep resumes
cleanly.

Mark the watchdog as suspended once the suspend ping succeeded, and ignore
userspace keepalives until the resume, so the pretimeout hrtimer stays
cancelled for the whole sleep.

Signed-off-by: zibao <zibao@proton.me>

--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_core.h
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_core.h
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@
 #define _WDOG_DEV_OPEN		0	/* Opened ? */
 #define _WDOG_ALLOW_RELEASE	1	/* Did we receive the magic char ? */
 #define _WDOG_KEEPALIVE		2	/* Did we receive a keepalive ? */
+#define _WDOG_SUSPENDED		3	/* Suspended ? */
 };
 
 /*
--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
@@ -195,6 +195,9 @@
 	if (!watchdog_hw_running(wdd))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (test_bit(_WDOG_SUSPENDED, &wd_data->status))
+		return 0;
+
 	set_bit(_WDOG_KEEPALIVE, &wd_data->status);
 
 	wd_data->last_keepalive = ktime_get();
@@ -1276,6 +1279,8 @@
 	mutex_lock(&wd_data->lock);
 	if (watchdog_worker_should_ping(wd_data))
 		ret = __watchdog_ping(wd_data->wdd);
+	if (!ret)
+		set_bit(_WDOG_SUSPENDED, &wd_data->status);
 	mutex_unlock(&wd_data->lock);
 
 	if (ret)
@@ -1299,6 +1304,8 @@
 	if (!wdd->wd_data)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	clear_bit(_WDOG_SUSPENDED, &wd_data->status);
+
 	/*
 	 * __watchdog_ping will also retrigger hrtimer and therefore restore the
 	 * ping worker if needed.
